    <string name="about_version">Version %1$s</string>
    <string name="about_desc">An audio visualizer and bass vibration for Android, inspired by the Pulse feature of EvolutionX ROMs. No root needed.</string>
    <string name="sec_how">How it works</string>
    <string name="how_1">Captures the sound that is playing (any music or video app) and analyzes its spectrum.</string>
    <string name="how_2">Draws the bars over other apps while music plays, and stops when it ends.</string>
    <string name="how_3">For vibration, it measures only the energy of the bass, not the overall volume.</string>
    <string name="how_4">It runs as an Accessibility service, with no permanent notification.</string>
    <string name="sec_privacy">Privacy</string>
    <string name="priv_1">No internet permission.</string>
    <string name="priv_2">Audio is analyzed on the device and never stored or sent.</string>
    <string name="priv_3">The service only reads the name of the app on screen, for the app filter. It does not read screen content.</string>
    <string name="sec_limits">Good to know</string>
    <string name="lim_1">Bars cannot be drawn on the always-on (ambient) screen. Vibration can work there.</string>
    <string name="lim_2">Some apps and ROMs block audio capture. The live meter shows whether it works.</string>
    <string name="lim_3">Audio processed by a DSP (ViPER4Android, JamesDSP) is usually captured after processing, but this depends on the device.</string>
    <string name="sec_help">Help</string>
    <string name="diag_note">If something does not work, copy the diagnostics and send it when asking for help. It contains no personal data.</string>
